{"answers":[{"question_id":"region_a>subregion_a1:d1","answer":"Yes. A1-HIA 4(1) supplies the Subregion A1 legal basis for the Article 8(2)(c) health-care route: the processing must be necessary for health care or treatment and carried out by or under the responsibility of a registered practitioner. The proposed second opinion is for deciding the patient's treatment, and Kestrel's consultant geneticists are registered practitioners. A1-HIA 5 separately imposes professional secrecy on registered practitioners handling health information. Because Harrow is a third party rather than an A1-HIA 4(2) agent, disclosure requires one of the Section 5(2) routes; the patient's specific consent supports that disclosure.

A1 law does not prevent reliance on the Article 8(2)(a) explicit-consent exception merely because the information is genetic and the purpose is treatment. Section 7 only prohibits consent from lifting the Article 8(1) prohibition where genetic information is processed for insurance or employment purposes. The treatment purpose therefore does not engage that additional prohibition. This does not remove the separate Section 7 restriction on using the Article 19(1)(a) consent derogation for an outward transfer of genetic information, addressed under d2.","facts":[{"fact_id":"f_987ab471487e","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_110e981b0a7c","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_827ad358a031","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_7892b94ae5e8","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_55ec68a77a25","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_66d5f3ce3996","path":"","quote":""}],"citations":["A1-HIA 2","A1-HIA 4","A1-HIA 5","A1-HIA 7"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 4#L1","requirement_ids":["healthcare_processing_basis","professional_secrecy_duty","third_party_disclosure_consent","genetic_insurance_employment_consent_bar"]},{"question_id":"region_a>subregion_a1:d2","answer":"The Section 6 notice, storage-encryption and key-location conditions do not apply to the arrangement as described. Section 6 is limited to an outward transfer by an A1 custodian of patient health records for hosting or storing them. Harrow keeps the referral in its own clinical record for its own patient care and does not host records for Kestrel or act as Kestrel's agent. Accordingly, this is not the Section 6 hosting or storage arrangement. The encrypted upload does not independently trigger Section 6, and A1 law imposes no Section 6 notice or key-location condition on this own-care referral.

However, A1-HIA 7 does limit the Article 19(1)(a) consent derogation. Genetic information may not be transferred outward on that basis. The facts state that Kestrel relies on the patient's explicit consent for the outward transfer, so that basis is unavailable under A1 law. The consent may still satisfy the A1 professional-secrecy disclosure condition, and A1-HIA 7 does not prohibit the transfer if another valid Region A outward-transfer route applies. Whether such another route is available is for the Region A specialist to determine.","facts":[{"fact_id":"f_3707d0e0f8a9","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_a7a94423ed89","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_d75ec85c160f","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_8c44c6e413c5","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_55ec68a77a25","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_6a3e2263dd33","path":"","quote":""}],"citations":["A1-HIA 5","A1-HIA 6","A1-HIA 7"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 7#L1","requirement_ids":["outward_hosting_storage_conditions","genetic_outward_transfer_basis","third_party_disclosure_consent"]},{"question_id":"region_a>subregion_a1:d3","answer":"No A1-HIA 8 impact-assessment category is engaged. Section 8 requires an assessment, regardless of the number of persons concerned, only for (a) hosting or storage of a patient record system by an agent outside Subregion A1, or (b) matching health information with information held by an insurer. Harrow is receiving the referral into its own clinical record for its own care, not hosting a patient record system as Kestrel's agent, and there is no insurer or insurer-information matching. The absence of an assessment for this one-off referral therefore does not breach the A1 list.","facts":[{"fact_id":"f_3707d0e0f8a9","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_a7a94423ed89","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_85110fb9a3e5","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_7ddb7b6d46db","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_2f7b22f9f431","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_7e86304fe561","path":"","quote":""}],"citations":["A1-HIA 8"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 8#L1","requirement_ids":["listed_impact_assessment"]}],"requirements":[{"id":"healthcare_processing_basis","title":"Health-care processing by or under a registered practitioner's responsibility","kind":"gate","status":"met","reasoning":"A1-HIA 4(1) makes health-information processing lawful for necessary health care or treatment when carried out by or under the responsibility of a registered practitioner. The proposed second opinion and consultation concern the patient's treatment, and Kestrel's consultant clinical geneticists are registered with the A1 Health Professions Board. The direct practitioner route is therefore met.","facts":[{"fact_id":"f_987ab471487e","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_110e981b0a7c","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_827ad358a031","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_7892b94ae5e8","path":"","quote":""}],"evidence_ids":[],"citations":["A1-HIA 2","A1-HIA 4"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 4#L1","routes":[{"name":"Direct processing by or under the responsibility of registered practitioners","status":"supported","reasoning":"Kestrel's processing is performed by its registered consultant clinical geneticists for diagnosis and treatment.","citations":["A1-HIA 4"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 4#L1"},{"name":"Processing by a qualifying agent on documented instructions","status":"ruled_out","reasoning":"The proposed arrangement is not an agent arrangement: Harrow keeps the information in its own clinical record for its own care and is not hosting records for Kestrel.","citations":["A1-HIA 4"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 4#L2"}],"missing_facts":[],"missing_evidence":[],"required_actions":[],"confirmations":[],"open_dependency":""},{"id":"professional_secrecy_duty","title":"Professional secrecy for health information obtained in practice","kind":"duty","status":"met","reasoning":"Section 5(1) imposes the duty on a registered practitioner in respect of health information obtained in the course of practice. The Kestrel practitioners are registered practitioners and are handling the patient's identified health and genetic information in their clinical practice. The duty applies throughout the processing.","facts":[{"fact_id":"f_987ab471487e","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_6a3e2263dd33","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_7892b94ae5e8","path":"","quote":""}],"evidence_ids":[],"citations":["A1-HIA 2","A1-HIA 5"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 5#L1","routes":[],"missing_facts":[],"missing_evidence":[],"required_actions":[],"confirmations":["The Section 5 duty applies to the Kestrel practitioners; A1-HIA 5 does not impose this A1 duty on Harrow's practitioners merely because Harrow receives the referral."],"open_dependency":""},{"id":"third_party_disclosure_consent","title":"Permitted disclosure of health information to the third-party specialist","kind":"gate","status":"met","reasoning":"Harrow is a third party for Section 5 purposes because it is not a qualifying agent under Section 4(2). Section 5(2) permits disclosure with the patient's consent. The consent record specifically identifies the named report, ECG summary, referral letter, Harrow clinic, and second-opinion purpose. That satisfies the A1 consent route for the proposed disclosure as described.","facts":[{"fact_id":"f_3707d0e0f8a9","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_66d5f3ce3996","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_5ec21466d488","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_cbbbb15c04e0","path":"","quote":""}],"evidence_ids":["ev_consent"],"citations":["A1-HIA 4","A1-HIA 5"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 5#L2","routes":[{"name":"Patient consent","status":"supported","reasoning":"The adult patient gave specific written consent to sending the identified referral materials to Harrow for a second opinion.","citations":["A1-HIA 5"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 5#L2"},{"name":"Disclosure required by law","status":"not_investigated","reasoning":"The current consent route already supports the disclosure; no separate legal requirement is asserted on the supplied facts.","citations":["A1-HIA 5"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 5#L2"},{"name":"Necessary to prevent a serious and imminent threat to life","status":"not_investigated","reasoning":"The current consent route already supports the disclosure, and the facts describe treatment planning rather than an asserted emergency threat-to-life disclosure.","citations":["A1-HIA 5"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 5#L2"},{"name":"Agent exception to third-party disclosure","status":"ruled_out","reasoning":"Harrow keeps the referral for its own care and is not acting only on Kestrel's documented instructions as an agent.","citations":["A1-HIA 4","A1-HIA 5"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 5#L3"}],"missing_facts":[],"missing_evidence":[],"required_actions":[],"confirmations":["Consent can be withdrawn by contacting Kestrel; the supplied A1 provisions do not prescribe an additional withdrawal procedure."],"open_dependency":""},{"id":"consent_age","title":"Minimum age for consent on the person's own behalf","kind":"gate","status":"met","reasoning":"A1-HIA 9 sets the age for consenting on one's own behalf at 14. The patient is an adult and the consent record is signed by the adult patient, so the A1 age threshold is met.","facts":[{"fact_id":"f_cbbbb15c04e0","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_5ec21466d488","path":"","quote":""}],"evidence_ids":["ev_consent"],"citations":["A1-HIA 9"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 9#L1","routes":[],"missing_facts":[],"missing_evidence":[],"required_actions":[],"confirmations":[],"open_dependency":""},{"id":"genetic_outward_transfer_basis","title":"No Article 19(1)(a) consent basis for an outward transfer of genetic information","kind":"gate","status":"unmet","reasoning":"A1-HIA 7 expressly provides that genetic information may not be made the subject of an outward transfer on the basis of Article 19(1)(a). The transfer contains genetic information, and the stated outward-transfer basis is the patient's explicit consent. As described, Kestrel is therefore relying on the A1-prohibited route.","facts":[{"fact_id":"f_72bdc3d5c28e","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_55ec68a77a25","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_66d5f3ce3996","path":"","quote":""}],"evidence_ids":["ev_consent"],"citations":["A1-HIA 7"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 7#L1","routes":[{"name":"Article 19(1)(a) explicit-consent derogation for genetic information","status":"ruled_out","reasoning":"A1-HIA 7 excludes this basis for an outward transfer concerning genetic information, regardless of the treatment purpose.","citations":["A1-HIA 7"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 7#L1"},{"name":"Another valid outward-transfer basis not relying on Article 19(1)(a)","status":"unresolved","reasoning":"A1-HIA 7 does not itself provide the alternative basis. Whether recognition, approved clauses, or another Region A route authorises this transfer must be determined under Region A law.","citations":["A1-HIA 7"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 7#L1"}],"missing_facts":[],"missing_evidence":[],"required_actions":["Do not make the genetic-information transfer on the Article 19(1)(a) consent derogation. Obtain and rely on a different outward-transfer basis if one is available under Region A law."],"confirmations":[],"open_dependency":"The Region A specialist must determine whether a non-Article 19(1)(a) outward-transfer route is available for this transfer."},{"id":"genetic_insurance_employment_consent_bar","title":"Genetic-information consent bar for insurance or employment processing","kind":"gate","status":"not_applicable","reasoning":"A1-HIA 7 also provides that consent may not lift the Article 8(1) prohibition for genetic information processed for insurance or employment purposes. The stated purpose is a patient's treatment and second opinion, not insurance or employment, so this A1 limitation is not engaged. A1 law therefore does not independently prevent the Article 8(2)(a) consent route on these facts.","facts":[{"fact_id":"f_fc5f59499494","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_110e981b0a7c","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_7892b94ae5e8","path":"","quote":""}],"evidence_ids":[],"citations":["A1-HIA 7"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 7#L1","routes":[{"name":"Consent for genetic information processed for insurance or employment purposes","status":"ruled_out","reasoning":"The condition that would activate this restriction—insurance or employment processing—is absent; the proposed processing is for treatment.","citations":["A1-HIA 7"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 7#L1"}],"missing_facts":[],"missing_evidence":[],"required_actions":[],"confirmations":[],"open_dependency":""},{"id":"outward_hosting_storage_conditions","title":"Notice, encryption and key-location conditions for outward hosting or storage","kind":"gate","status":"not_applicable","reasoning":"Section 6(1) applies only where an A1-established custodian makes an outward transfer of patient health records for hosting or storing them. Harrow stores the referral in its own clinical record for its own patient care and does not store records on Kestrel's behalf. The proposed transfer is therefore outside the Section 6 scope. No A1-HIA 6 notice, at-rest encryption, or Region A-only decryption-key condition is required for this arrangement.","facts":[{"fact_id":"f_3707d0e0f8a9","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_a7a94423ed89","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_8c44c6e413c5","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_d75ec85c160f","path":"","quote":""}],"evidence_ids":[],"citations":["A1-HIA 2","A1-HIA 6"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 6#L1","routes":[{"name":"Outward hosting or storage by an agent for the A1 custodian","status":"ruled_out","reasoning":"The recipient is not acting as Kestrel's agent or external host; it retains the referral in its own clinical record for its own care.","citations":["A1-HIA 6"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 6#L1"},{"name":"Recipient's own clinical record for its own care","status":"supported","reasoning":"The supplied arrangement is an independent clinical referral and own-care record, not hosting or storage for Kestrel.","citations":["A1-HIA 6"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 6#L1"}],"missing_facts":[],"missing_evidence":[],"required_actions":[],"confirmations":["The encryption used for the upload does not convert the own-care referral into Section 6 hosting or storage."],"open_dependency":""},{"id":"listed_impact_assessment","title":"Impact assessment for listed processing","kind":"duty","status":"not_applicable","reasoning":"A1-HIA 8 lists only two relevant categories: hosting or storage of a patient record system by an agent outside A1, and matching health information with information held by an insurer. Harrow is not an agent or external host and is keeping the referral for its own care; there is also no insurer and no insurer-information matching. The one-off nature and single-patient scale do not change this conclusion, because neither listed category is present.","facts":[{"fact_id":"f_3707d0e0f8a9","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_a7a94423ed89","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_85110fb9a3e5","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_2f7b22f9f431","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_7e86304fe561","path":"","quote":""}],"evidence_ids":[],"citations":["A1-HIA 8"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 8#L1","routes":[{"name":"Hosting or storage of a patient record system by an agent outside Subregion A1","status":"ruled_out","reasoning":"Harrow is not storing records as Kestrel's agent or hosting Kestrel's patient record system.","citations":["A1-HIA 8"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 8#L2"},{"name":"Matching health information with information held by an insurer","status":"ruled_out","reasoning":"The recipient is a health-care provider, not an insurer, and the proposed processing contains no insurer matching.","citations":["A1-HIA 8"],"quote_id":"A1-HIA 8#L3"}],"missing_facts":[],"missing_evidence":[],"required_actions":[],"confirmations":[],"open_dependency":""}]}

